{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.canonical_weight_systems_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.canonical_weight_systems_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L119-L128","doc":"**The three canonical weight systems are distinct.** Normalising each\nprojector diagonal by its trace gives three *different* normalised weight systems\non the color pairs (`A`: all mass on same-color; `T₁`: all on different-color;\n`H`: split). So the isotypic decomposition genuinely narrows `W` — it is not\nthree names for one weighting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.uniform_is_isotypy_blind_barycentre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.uniform_is_isotypy_blind_barycentre","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**The uniform projection `W = 1/9` is the isotypy-blind barycentre.** The\nthree projectors sum to the identity, whose diagonal is `1` on every pair; so\ndividing the summed diagonal by 9 returns exactly `1/9` on both pair classes.\nThe \"flavor-only projection\" the conjecture identifies as lossy is precisely the\naverage that forgets which isotypic summand a pair sits in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.projector_traces_eq_dims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.projector_traces_eq_dims","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L100-L108","doc":"**Projector traces recover the summand dimensions.** For each summand,\n`3·diag(same) + 6·diag(diff) = dim`. A genuine consistency check on the projector\ndata: wrong diagonals would not reproduce `1, 3, 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.diagDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.diagDiff","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L97-L98","doc":"Projector-diagonal entry on a **different-color** pair, per summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.diagSame","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.diagSame","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L94-L95","doc":"Projector-diagonal entry on a **same-color** pair, per summand `A, T₁, H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.alt_summand_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.alt_summand_forced","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L82-L86","doc":"The complementary statement: exactly one sublist sums to `dim Alt² = 3`,\nnamely `[3]` — the `T₁` summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.sym_alt_assignment_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.sym_alt_assignment_forced","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L71-L80","doc":"**The Sym²/Alt² assignment is FORCED by dimension.** Among the sub-collections\nof the summand dimensions `{1, 3, 5}`, exactly one sums to `dim Sym² = 6`, namely\n`{1, 5}` — so `Sym² T₁ = A ⊕ H` and, by complementation, `Alt² T₁ = T₁`. The\n`Z/2` grading of the 9 color pairs is therefore determined, not chosen.\n\nStated as: of the eight sublists of `[1,3,5]`, the ones summing to `6` are\nexactly `[1,5]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.sym_alt_dims_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.sym_alt_dims_partition","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L68-L69","doc":"`Sym²` and `Alt²` partition the tensor square: `6 + 3 = 9`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.tensor_dim_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.tensor_dim_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L64-L66","doc":"**Dimension consistency.** The summand dimensions sum to `dim(T₁)² = 9`.\nFalsifiable: a decomposition `A ⊕ T₁ ⊕ G` would give `1 + 3 + 4 = 8 ≠ 9`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.altSquareDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.altSquareDim","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L59-L60","doc":"`dim Alt²(V)` for `dim V = 3`, i.e. `3·2/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.symSquareDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.symSquareDim","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L56-L57","doc":"`dim Sym²(V)` for `dim V = 3`, i.e. `3·4/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.summandDims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.summandDims","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorPairIsotypicDecomposition.lean#L52-L54","doc":"Dimensions of the three summands of `T₁ ⊗ T₁`, in the order `A, T₁, H`, as\ncomputed by the exact character decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}